# 7. Different creation routes

## Full Variation Points editor

The **Add Variation Point** button asks for the complete definition:

1. Name
2. Kind
3. Target type
4. Target IDs
5. Feature expression
6. Typed conditions
7. Property path, when applicable
8. Realization domain
9. Initial value-rule expression, when applicable
10. Initial value-rule typed conditions
11. Realized value

## Graph interaction

- Double-click element body → presets **Existence**
- Double-click a displayed parameter → presets **Primitive Property** and its parameter path
- Double-click displayed duration → presets **Primitive Property** and `metadata:duration`
- Double-click tags → presets **Primitive Tag** and `tags`
- Double-click connector → asks between **Existence** and **Primitive Property**

## 150% Preview quick creator

The quick creator asks for fewer inputs:

- Feature expression
- Name
- Realized value for modification kinds

It does not initially ask for:

- Typed feature-value conditions
- Realization domain
- Full rule structure

Those can be added afterward through the full Variation Points editor.

There is also a current limitation: creating a connector property variation directly from the 150% Preview does not ask for the relationship property path. The resulting definition must be completed through **Variation Points → Edit** before it is valid.

# 8. Methodology elements not implemented

| Methodology capability | REV03 status | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Existence | Implemented | Essential 150% → 100% functionality |
| Primitive Property | Implemented with whitelist | Safe scalar modification |
| Primitive Tag | Implemented with whitelist | Supports tags/custom attributes |
| Element Property | Implemented with limited ID retargeting | Safe reference modification |
| Element Tag | Not implemented | The project has no element-valued profile-tag model |
| Arbitrary script expressions | Intentionally excluded | Browser safety and deterministic execution |
| Automatic blank-expression inference from Feature Impacts | Not implemented | No separate Feature Impacts collection |
| General UML property/tag discovery | Not implemented | The workbench uses a bounded data model |
| Replace and Rewire | Not implemented as separate kinds | Limited connector retargeting is available through Element Property |

The official documentation defines the four implemented kinds plus Element Tag and describes Primitive/Element value specifications. [No Magic variation-point kinds](https://docs.nomagic.com/spaces/PLE2021x/pages/64973711/Defining%2Bsystem%2Bmodel%2Busing%2Bvariation%2Bpoints) The overall methodology remains feature model → configuration → variation points in the 150% model → 100% realization. [No Magic MBPLE overview](https://docs.nomagic.com/spaces/PLE2021x/pages/64973700/Model-Based%2BProduct%2BLine%2BEngineering)
